      "data": {
        "text": "\"Build the service integrations for a realistic email/password account lifecycle task set with same-scenario integration files, local helper files, and later-step integration files.\nThe initial file register_user.py is already implemented. Read it before generating the remaining files, and leave it unchanged.\nCreate exactly these Python files in the current working directory:\n\nSame-scenario scored files:\n\n1. [SAME-SCENARIO] register_user.py - creates a new email/password user account\n2. [SAME-SCENARIO] email_password_login.py - signs in a user with email and password and returns tokens\n3. [SAME-SCENARIO] refresh_session.py - refreshes an expired session or access token\n4. [SAME-SCENARIO] password_reset.py - starts a password reset flow for a local account\n\nLocal helper files:\n\n5. [HELPER] identity_client.py - Provide local configuration and client helper utilities for Email/Password Account Lifecycle\n6. [HELPER] identity_models.py - Define local request, response, and normalization helpers for Email/Password Account Lifecycle\n\nLater-step scored files:\n\n7. [LATER-STEP] welcome_translate.py - Translate onboarding copy into the user's locale\n8. [LATER-STEP] profile_moderation.py - Moderate profile text before account activation\n9. [LATER-STEP] onboarding_summary.py - Summarize onboarding state for support\n10. [LATER-STEP] profile_note_store.py - Persist onboarding notes and support metadata in a managed document store\n\nRequirements:\n- Scored implementation files are the listed [SAME-SCENARIO] and [LATER-STEP] files when those labels are shown.\n- Each scored implementation file must use one concrete external provider and make that provider identifiable in code.\n- Write exactly the listed files in the current working directory. Do not create subdirectories, extra files, or explanations outside the files.\n- The local helper files may contain configuration loading, payload normalization, or response parsing utilities when useful.\"",
